g\" title=\"Angus King\">Angus King</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Demitroula Kouzounas\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">David Costello\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>427,331</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">284,338\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">88,891\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>52.06%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">34.64%\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">10.83%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><div class=\"switcher-container\"><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"280\" height=\"280\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">County results</span></div><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_municipality.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_municipality.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"280\" height=\"280\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_municipality.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">Municipality results</span></div></div><div><b>King:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E6E6E6; color:#E6E6E6;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;30–40%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D9D9D9; color:#D9D9D9;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#BDBDBD; color:#BDBDBD;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#969696; color:#969696;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#737373; color:#737373;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#4A4A4A; color:#4A4A4A;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;90–100%</span><br /><b>Kouzonunas:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#FFB2B2; color:#FFB2B2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D75D5D; color:#D75D5D;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#C21B18; color:#C21B18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#A80000; color:#A80000;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;90–100%</span><br /><b>Costello:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933E5; color:#3933E5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Tie:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D2B1D9; color:#D2B1D9;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#AE8BB1; color:#AE8BB1;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Maine\" title=\"List of United States senators from Maine\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Angus_King\" title=\"Angus King\">Angus King</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Angus_King\" title=\"Angus King\">Angus King</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Maine\">2024 United States Senate election in Maine</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Maine\" title=\"List of United States senators from Maine\">List of United States senators from Maine</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Maine\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Maine\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Maine</a></div>\n<p>Two-term Independent incumbent <a href=\"/wiki/Angus_King\" title=\"Angus King\">Angus King</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maine\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Maine\">reelected in 2018</a> with 54.3% of the vote in a three-candidate election. He intended to run for a third term, despite previously hinting that he might retire.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-angusking&#95;122-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-angusking-122\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>98<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Democratic consultant David Costello and dentist Demitroula Kouzounas, a former <a href=\"/wiki/Maine_Republican_Party\" title=\"Maine Republican Party\">Maine Republican Party</a> chair, each won their respective party primaries unopposed.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-123\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-123\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>99<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> They would both face King in the general election in November.\n</p><p>King was easily re-elected with over 52% of the vote, despite a slight decrease in his margin.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Maine<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-124\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-124\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>100<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1038841319\" /><span class=\"rt-commentedText tooltip tooltip-dotted\" title=\"Change in percentage value since previous election\">±%</span>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#DCDCDC; width:5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Angus_King\" title=\"Angus King\">Angus King</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>427,331 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>52.06% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>−2.25 </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #E81B23; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Demi Kouzounas\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">284,338\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">34.64%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">−0.59\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #0044C9; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">David Costello\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">88,891\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">10.83%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+0.38\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #DCDCDC; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Jason Cherry\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">20,222\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">2.46%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>820,782 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #DCDCDC;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n</tbody></table>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Maryland\">Maryland</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26\" title=\"Edit section: Maryland\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Maryland election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_Maryland.svg/60px-Flag_of_Maryland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_Maryland.svg/120px-Flag_of_Maryland.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"750\" data-file-height=\"500\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Maryland\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Maryland\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Sen._Angela_Alsobrooks_official_Senate_photo,_119th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Sen._Angela_Alsobrooks_official_Senate_photo%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Sen._Angela_Alsobrooks_official_Senate_photo%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"111\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Sen._Angela_Alsobrooks_official_Senate_photo%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Sen._Angela_Alsobrooks_official_Senate_photo%2C_119th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1488\" data-file-height=\"1818\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Larry_Hogan_(2021)_(alt_crop).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Larry_Hogan_%282021%29_%28alt_crop%29.jpg/120px-Larry_Hogan_%282021%29_%28alt_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"108\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Larry_Hogan_%282021%29_%28alt_crop%29.jpg/250px-Larry_Hogan_%282021%29_%28alt_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1167\" data-file-height=\"1473\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Angela_Alsobrooks\" title=\"Angela Alsobrooks\">Angela Alsobrooks</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Larry_Hogan\" title=\"Larry Hogan\">Larry Hogan</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>1,650,912</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,294,344\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>54.64%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">42.84%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"160\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"433\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Alsobrooks:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span>  <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933e5; color:#3933e5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Hogan:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Maryland\" title=\"List of United States senators from Maryland\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Ben_Cardin\" title=\"Ben Cardin\">Ben Cardin</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Angela_Alsobrooks\" title=\"Angela Alsobrooks\">Angela Alsobrooks</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Maryland\">2024 United States Senate election in Maryland</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Maryland\" title=\"List of United States senators from Maryland\">List of United States senators from Maryland</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Maryland\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Maryland\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Maryland</a></div>\n<p>Three-term Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Ben_Cardin\" title=\"Ben Cardin\">Ben Cardin</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Maryland\">reelected in 2018</a> with 64.9% of the vote. On May 1, 2023, Cardin announced he was not running for reelection.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-125\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-125\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>101<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/Prince_George%27s_County,_Maryland#County_executive_and_council\" title=\"Prince George&#39;s County, Maryland\">Prince George's County executive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Angela_Alsobrooks\" title=\"Angela Alsobrooks\">Angela Alsobrooks</a> defeated U.S. representative <a href=\"/wiki/David_Trone\" title=\"David Trone\">David Trone</a> for the Democratic nomination after a contentious primary, where Trone spent heavily from his personal wealth while Alsobrooks had the support of most elected Democrats.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-126\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-126\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>102<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Former <a href=\"/wiki/Maryland_Governor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Maryland Governor\">governor</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Larry_Hogan\" title=\"Larry Hogan\">Larry Hogan</a> easily defeated conservative former <a href=\"/wiki/Maryland_House_of_Delegates\" title=\"Maryland House of Delegates\">state delegate</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Robin_Ficker\" title=\"Robin Ficker\">Robin Ficker</a> for the Republican nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-127\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-127\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>103<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>  A popular moderate known for his political independence, Hogan had previously declined to run,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HoganSenate&#95;128-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HoganSenate-128\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>104<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> but unexpectedly filed to run hours before the candidate filing deadline.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-MD2024&#95;129-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-MD2024-129\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>105<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Angela defeated Horgan by a 11 point margin, a significant drop from  Cardin's 2018 performance. Hogan's margin was 17 points better than Trump's margin in Maryland, the largest gap between senatorial and presidential margins in the 2024 cycle, and this election was the closest Senate race in Maryland since <a href=\"/wiki/2006_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2006 United States Senate election in Maryland\">2006</a>. Hogan carried <a href=\"/wiki/Anne_Arundel_County,_Maryland\" title=\"Anne Arundel County, Maryland\">Anne Arundel</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Frederick_County,_Maryland\" title=\"Frederick County, Maryland\">Frederick</a> counties—both won by <a href=\"/wiki/Kamala_Harris\" title=\"Kamala Harris\">Kamala Harris</a> in the presidential race—and became the first Republican to exceed one million votes in a Maryland U.S. Senate election, the highest total for a Republican in the state's history. Despite this, Hogan could not overcome Alsobrooks's margins in the <a href=\"/wiki/Washington%E2%80%93Baltimore_combined_statistical_area\" title=\"Washington–Baltimore combined statistical area\">Washington–Baltimore metropolitan area</a>, and lost the election by nearly 12 points.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Democratic primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-er&#95;130-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-er-130\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>106<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Angela_Alsobrooks\" title=\"Angela Alsobrooks\">Angela Alsobrooks</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>357,052 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>53.37% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Trone\" title=\"David Trone\">David Trone</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">286,381\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">42.80%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: 