lass=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>106<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Larry_Hogan\" title=\"Larry Hogan\">Larry Hogan</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>183,661 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>64.18% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Robin_Ficker\" title=\"Robin Ficker\">Robin Ficker</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">79,517\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">27.79%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Chris Chaffee\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">9,134\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">3.19%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Lorie Friend\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">5,867\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">2.05%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">John A. Myrick\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">4,987\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">1.74%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Moe Barakat\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">2,203\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">0.77%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Laban Seyoum\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">782\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">0.27%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>286,151 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Maryland<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-131\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-131\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>107<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1038841319\" /><span class=\"rt-commentedText tooltip tooltip-dotted\" title=\"Change in percentage value since previous election\">±%</span>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9; width:5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Angela_Alsobrooks\" title=\"Angela Alsobrooks\">Angela Alsobrooks</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>1,650,912 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>54.64% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>−10.22% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #E81B23; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Larry_Hogan\" title=\"Larry Hogan\">Larry Hogan</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">1,294,344\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">42.84%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+12.53%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #fed000; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Libertarian_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Libertarian Party (United States)\">Libertarian</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Mike Scott\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">69,396\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">2.30%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+1.30%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: white; width: 2px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"/wiki/Write-in_candidate\" title=\"Write-in candidate\">Write-in</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">6,726\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">0.22%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">+0.12%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>3,021,378 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #0044C9;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n</tbody></table>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Massachusetts\">Massachusetts</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27\" title=\"Edit section: Massachusetts\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Massachusetts election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg/60px-Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg/120px-Flag_of_Massachusetts.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1500\" data-file-height=\"900\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Massachusetts\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Massachusetts\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Elizabeth_Warren,_official_portrait,_114th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Elizabeth_Warren%2C_official_portrait%2C_114th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Elizabeth_Warren%2C_official_portrait%2C_114th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"93\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Elizabeth_Warren%2C_official_portrait%2C_114th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Elizabeth_Warren%2C_official_portrait%2C_114th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1102\" data-file-height=\"1615\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:John_Deaton,_2024.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/John_Deaton%2C_2024.jpg/120px-John_Deaton%2C_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/John_Deaton%2C_2024.jpg/250px-John_Deaton%2C_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"657\" data-file-height=\"876\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_Warren\" title=\"Elizabeth Warren\">Elizabeth Warren</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">John Deaton\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>2,041,668</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,365,440\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>59.81%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">40.00%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><div class=\"switcher-container\"><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"186\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"502\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" data-switcher-default=\"\" style=\"display:none\">County results</span></div><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_Election_in_Massachusetts_by_Municipality.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/2024_United_States_Senate_Election_in_Massachusetts_by_Municipality.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_Election_in_Massachusetts_by_Municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"186\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/2024_United_States_Senate_Election_in_Massachusetts_by_Municipality.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_Election_in_Massachusetts_by_Municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"502\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">Municipality results</span></div></div><div><b>Warren:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933e5; color:#3933e5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#0D0596; color:#0D0596;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;90–100%</span><br /><b>Deaton:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Massachusetts\" title=\"List of United States senators from Massachusetts\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_Warren\" title=\"Elizabeth Warren\">Elizabeth Warren</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_Warren\" title=\"Elizabeth Warren\">Elizabeth Warren</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Massachusetts\">2024 United States Senate election in Massachusetts</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Massachusetts\" title=\"List of United States senators from Massachusetts\">List of United States senators from Massachusetts</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Massachusetts\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Massachusetts\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Massachusetts</a></div>\n<p>Two-term Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_Warren\" title=\"Elizabeth Warren\">Elizabeth Warren</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Massachusetts\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Massachusetts\">reelected in 2018</a> with 60.3% of the vote. On March 27, 2023, Warren announced that she was running for reelection.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-132\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-132\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>108<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Software company owner Robert Antonellis,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-133\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-133\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>109<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Quincy,_Massachusetts\" title=\"Quincy, Massachusetts\">Quincy</a> City Council president Ian Cain,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-134\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-134\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>110<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> and attorney John Deaton<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-135\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-135\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>111<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> ran as Republicans.\n</p><p>Though Warren won by 19 points, this  election marked the first time that she had lost <a href=\"/wiki/Bristol_County,_Massachusetts\" title=\"Bristol County, Massachusetts\">Bristol County</a> while running for the office. Warren underperformed <a href=\"/wiki/Kamala_Harris\" title=\"Kamala Harris\">Kamala Harris</a> by 6 points in the concurrent <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election_in_Massachusetts\" title=\"2024 United States presidential election in Massachusetts\">presidential election</a>, making her the second-worst Democratic Senate performer in the 2024 cycle after <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Maryland\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Maryland\">Angela Alsobrooks</a> in Maryland.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-p2024&#95;136-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-p2024-136\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>112<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b>John Deaton </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>136,773 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>64.51% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Robert Antonellis\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">54,940\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">25.91%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Ian Cain\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">19,374\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">9.14%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #FFFFFF; width: 2px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"/wiki/Write-in_candidate\" title=\"Write-in candidate\">Write-in</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">924\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">0.44%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>212,011 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Massachusetts<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-137\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-137\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>113<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1038841319\" /><span class=\"rt-commentedText tooltip tooltip-dotted\" title=\"Change in percentage value since previous election\">±%</span>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9; width:5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Elizabeth_Warren\" title=\"Elizabeth Warren\">Elizabeth Warren</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>2,041,668 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>59.81% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>−0.53 </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #E81B23; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">John Deaton\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">1,365,440\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">40.00%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+3.83\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: white; width: 2px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"/wiki/Write-in_candidate\" title=\"Write-in candidate\">Write-in</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">6,221\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">0.18%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">+0.08\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>3,413,329 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #0044C9;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n</tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Michigan\">Michigan</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28\" title=\"Edit section: Michigan\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Michigan election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Flag_of_Michigan.svg/60px-Flag_of_Michigan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Flag_of_Michigan.svg/120px-Flag_of_Michigan.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"342\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Michigan\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Michigan\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Elissa_Slotkin,_official_portrait,_116th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Elissa_Slotkin%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Elissa_Slotkin%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"105\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Elissa_Slotkin%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Elissa_Slotkin%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1936\" data-file-height=\"2508\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_(3x4_cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/120px-Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg/250px-Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_%283x4_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"822\" data-file-height=\"1099\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Elissa_Slotkin\" title=\"Elissa Slotkin\">Elissa Slotkin</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)\">Mike Rogers</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>2,712,686</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">2,693,680\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>48.64%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">48.30%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Slotkin:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#a5b0ff; color:#a5b0ff;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40-50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span><br /><b>Rogers:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#ffb2b2; color:#ffb2b2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#e27f7f; color:#e27f7f;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d72f30; color:#d72f30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Michigan\" title=\"List of United States senators from Michigan\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Debbie_Stabenow\" title=\"Debbie Stabenow\">Debbie Stabenow</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Elissa_Slotkin\" title=\"Elissa Slotkin\">Elissa Slotkin</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Michigan\">2024 United States Senate election in Michigan</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Michigan\" title=\"List of United States senators from Michigan\">List of United States senators from Michigan</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Michigan\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Michigan\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Michigan</a></div>\n<p>Four-term Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Debbie_Stabenow\" title=\"Debbie Stabenow\">Debbie Stabenow</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Michigan\">reelected in 2018</a> with 52.3% of the vote. She announced on January 5, 2023, that she would retire, and would not run for a fifth term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-StabenowMI&#95;21-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-StabenowMI-21\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>16<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Representative <a href=\"/wiki/Elissa_Slotkin\" title=\"Elissa Slotkin\">Elissa Slotkin</a> and actor <a href=\"/wiki/Hill_Harper\" title=\"Hill Harper\">Hill Harper</a> ran for the Democratic nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-138\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-138\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>114<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-139\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-139\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>115<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Former U.S. representatives <a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)\">Mike Rogers</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Justin_Amash\" title=\"Justin Amash\">Justin Amash</a>, and hedge fund manager Sandy Pensler<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-140\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-140\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>116<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> ran for the Republican nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-141\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-141\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>117<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Meijer&#95;142-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Meijer-142\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>118<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-143\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-143\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>119<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-144\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-144\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>120<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> The nominees were Slotkin and Rogers, who easily won their primaries as expected.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p><p>Stolki narrowly defeated Rogers in general election by a 0.34% margin. Stolki won 48.64% of the vote compared to Rogers' 48.3%. On November 6, 2024, major news organizations projected that Slotkin had won the election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-145\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-145\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-146\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-146\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>122<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-147\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-147\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>123<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Slotkin received 23,847 fewer votes than <a href=\"/wiki/Kamala_Harris\" title=\"Kamala Harris\">Kamala Harris</a>, while Rogers received 122,956 fewer votes than <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\">Donald Trump</a>. As Republican presidential nominee <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\">Donald Trump</a> carried Michigan on the same ballot, this was the first time Michigan voted for candidates of different political parties for U.S. senator and president since Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Riegle\" title=\"Donald Riegle\">Don Riegle</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/1988_United_States_Senate_election_in_Michigan\" title=\"1988 United States Senate election in Michigan\">re-elected</a> as Republican <a href=\"/wiki/George_H._W._Bush\" title=\"George H. W. Bush\">George H. W. Bush</a> carried the state in <a href=\"/wiki/1988_United_States_presidential_election\" title=\"1988 United States presidential election\">1988</a>.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Democratic primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-mi&#95;148-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-mi-148\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Elissa_Slotkin\" title=\"Elissa Slotkin\">Elissa Slotkin</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>712,791 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>76.33% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Hill_Harper\" title=\"Hill Harper\">Hill Harper</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">221,053\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">23.67%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>933,844 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-mi&#95;148-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-mi-148\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Republican Party (US)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Mike_Rogers_(Michigan_politician)\" title=\"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)\">Mike Rogers</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>555,766 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>63.19% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Republican Party (US)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Justin_Amash\" title=\"Justin Amash\">Justin Amash</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">137,565\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">15.64%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Republican Party (US)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Sherry O'Donnell\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">106,466\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">12.10%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Republican Party (US)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Sandy Pensler (<i>withdrawn</i>)\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">79,772\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">9.07%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>879,569 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Michigan<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-149\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-149\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>125<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=