g.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Ty Pinkins\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>763,420</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">451,981\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>62.81%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">37.19%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi_results_map_by_county.svg/250px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"240\" height=\"363\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi_results_map_by_county.svg/500px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"535\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Wicker:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#C21B18; color:#C21B18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Pinkins:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Mississippi\" title=\"List of United States senators from Mississippi\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Mississippi\">2024 United States Senate election in Mississippi</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Mississippi\" title=\"List of United States senators from Mississippi\">List of United States senators from Mississippi</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Mississippi\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Mississippi\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Mississippi</a></div>\n<p>Two-term Republican <a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Mississippi\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Mississippi\">reelected in 2018</a> with 58.5% of the vote. Wicker ran for a third full term. He faced a primary challenge from conservative <a href=\"/wiki/Mississippi_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Mississippi House of Representatives\">state representative</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Dan_Eubanks\" title=\"Dan Eubanks\">Dan Eubanks</a> and won by a comfortable margin.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-154\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-154\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>130<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Wicker would face Democratic lawyer Ty Pinkins in the general election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-Ty&#95;155-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Ty-155\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>131<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Wicker easily won re-election by a 25 point margin, improving his previous performances.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-156\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-156\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>132<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Mississippi_Republican_Party\" title=\"Mississippi Republican Party\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>152,086 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>61.40% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mississippi_Republican_Party\" title=\"Mississippi Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Ghannon Burton\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">61,387\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">24.78%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mississippi_Republican_Party\" title=\"Mississippi Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Dan_Eubanks\" title=\"Dan Eubanks\">Dan Eubanks</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">34,238\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">13.82%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>247,711 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Mississippi<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-157\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-157\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>133<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1038841319\" /><span class=\"rt-commentedText tooltip tooltip-dotted\" title=\"Change in percentage value since previous election\">±%</span>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23; width:5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Roger_Wicker\" title=\"Roger Wicker\">Roger Wicker</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>763,420 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>62.81% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>+4.32% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #0044C9; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Ty Pinkins\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">451,981\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">37.19%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">−2.28%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>1,215,401 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #E81B23;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Missouri\">Missouri</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31\" title=\"Edit section: Missouri\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Missouri election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Flag_of_Missouri.svg/60px-Flag_of_Missouri.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"29\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Flag_of_Missouri.svg/120px-Flag_of_Missouri.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2400\" data-file-height=\"1400\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Missouri\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Missouri\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Josh_Hawley,_official_portrait,_116th_congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Josh_Hawley%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Josh_Hawley%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Josh_Hawley%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Josh_Hawley%2C_official_portrait%2C_116th_congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2051\" data-file-height=\"2736\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Lucas_Kunce_(Machinists_Union_Rally)_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lucas_Kunce_%28Machinists_Union_Rally%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Lucas_Kunce_%28Machinists_Union_Rally%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Lucas_Kunce_%28Machinists_Union_Rally%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Lucas_Kunce_%28Machinists_Union_Rally%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"988\" data-file-height=\"1318\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Josh_Hawley\" title=\"Josh Hawley\">Josh Hawley</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lucas_Kunce\" title=\"Lucas Kunce\">Lucas Kunce</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>1,651,907</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,243,728\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>55.57%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">41.84%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"266\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"717\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Hawley:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#ffb2b2; color:#ffb2b2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d72f30; color:#d72f30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#c21b18; color:#c21b18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Kunce:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#A5B0FF; color:#A5B0FF;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933e5; color:#3933e5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Missouri\" title=\"List of United States senators from Missouri\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Josh_Hawley\" title=\"Josh Hawley\">Josh Hawley</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Josh_Hawley\" title=\"Josh Hawley\">Josh Hawley</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Missouri\">2024 United States Senate election in Missouri</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Missouri\" title=\"List of United States senators from Missouri\">List of United States senators from Missouri</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Missouri\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Missouri\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Missouri</a></div>\n<p>One-term Republican <a href=\"/wiki/Josh_Hawley\" title=\"Josh Hawley\">Josh Hawley</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Missouri\">elected in 2018</a> with 51.4% of the vote. Hawley ran for a second term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HawleyRunning&#95;158-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HawleyRunning-158\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>134<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Marine veteran <a href=\"/wiki/Lucas_Kunce\" title=\"Lucas Kunce\">Lucas Kunce</a>, who ran unsuccessfully for the Class III seat in <a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Missouri#Democratic_primary\" title=\"2022 United States Senate election in Missouri\">2022</a>,  won the Democratic nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-159\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-159\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>135<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Hawley defeated Kunce to win reelection by a 14 point margin, a significant improvement from his 6 point margin in 2018.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">&#91;<i><a href=\"/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i>&#93;</sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Democratic primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-p86&#95;160-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-p86-160\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>136<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Lucas_Kunce\" title=\"Lucas Kunce\">Lucas Kunce</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>255,775 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>67.64% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Karla_May\" title=\"Karla May\">Karla May</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">87,908\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">23.25%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">December Harmon\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">26,804\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">7.09%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Mita Biswas\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">7,647\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">2.02%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>378,134 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Missouri<sup id=\"c