ed States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Jacky_Rosen\" title=\"Jacky Rosen\">Jacky Rosen</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>701,105 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>47.87% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>−2.54% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #E81B23; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sam_Brown_(military)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Sam Brown (military)\">Sam Brown</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">677,046\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">46.22%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+0.84%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"background-color: white; width: 2px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"/wiki/None_of_These_Candidates\" title=\"None of These Candidates\">None of These Candidates</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">44,380\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">3.03%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">+1.46%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #c49334; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_American_Party_of_Nevada\" title=\"Independent American Party of Nevada\">Independent American</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Janine Hansen\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">21,316\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">1.46%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+0.73%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #fed000; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Libertarian_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Libertarian Party (United States)\">Libertarian</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Chris Cunningham\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">20,881\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">1.43%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+0.48%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>1,464,728 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #0044C9;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n</tbody></table>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"New_Jersey\">New Jersey</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=37\" title=\"Edit section: New Jersey\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:280px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">New Jersey election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg/60px-Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg/120px-Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"600\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Sen_Andy_Kim_118th_Congress_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sen_Andy_Kim_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Sen_Andy_Kim_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sen_Andy_Kim_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Sen_Andy_Kim_118th_Congress_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"600\" data-file-height=\"800\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Curtis_Bashaw_2024.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Curtis_Bashaw_2024.jpg/120px-Curtis_Bashaw_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Curtis_Bashaw_2024.jpg/250px-Curtis_Bashaw_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"900\" data-file-height=\"1200\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Andy_Kim_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Andy Kim (politician)\">Andy Kim</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Curtis Bashaw\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>2,161,491</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,773,589\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>53.61%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">43.99%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><div class=\"switcher-container\"><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"280\" height=\"280\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">County results</span></div><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_municipality.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_municipality.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"280\" height=\"280\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_municipality.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span> <span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">Municipality results</span></div></div><div><b>Kim:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#A5B0FF; color:#A5B0FF;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996E2; color:#7996E2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933E5; color:#3933E5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#0D0596; color:#0D0596;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;&gt;90%</span><br /><b>Bashaw:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#FFB2B2; color:#FFB2B2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D75D5D; color:#D75D5D;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#C21B18; color:#C21B18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Jersey\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Jersey\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/George_Helmy\" title=\"George Helmy\">George Helmy</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Andy_Kim_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Andy Kim (politician)\">Andy Kim</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">2024 United States Senate election in New Jersey</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_New_Jersey\" title=\"List of United States senators from New Jersey\">List of United States senators from New Jersey</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in New Jersey\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in New Jersey</a></div>\n<p>Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Bob_Menendez\" title=\"Bob Menendez\">Bob Menendez</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_New_Jersey\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in New Jersey\">reelected in 2018</a> with 54.0% of the vote. On July 13, 2021, <i>The New Jersey Globe</i> reported that Menendez planned to run for a fourth full term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-menendezrunning&#95;176-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-menendezrunning-176\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>152<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-newjerseyglobe.com&#95;177-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-newjerseyglobe.com-177\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>153<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> On September 22, 2023, Menendez was indicted on federal <a href=\"/wiki/Bribery\" title=\"Bribery\">bribery</a> charges.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-178\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-178\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>154<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> On March 14, 2024, a week after his planned retirement, Menendez reversed his decision and attempted to run for re-election as an Independent candidate.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-179\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-179\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>155<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Following his conviction on July 16, he announced that he would resign on August 20 and suspend his candidacy.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-180\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-180\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>156<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-181\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-181\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>157<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Governor <a href=\"/wiki/Phil_Murphy\" title=\"Phil Murphy\">Phil Murphy</a> announced that day he would appoint <a href=\"/wiki/George_Helmy\" title=\"George Helmy\">George Helmy</a>, his former chief of staff, to serve as the <a href=\"/wiki/Caretaker_government#Caretakers\" title=\"Caretaker government\">caretaker</a> before the election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-182\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-182\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>158<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Financier and current first lady of New Jersey <a href=\"/wiki/Tammy_Murphy\" title=\"Tammy Murphy\">Tammy Murphy</a> also ran for the Democratic nomination, but ended her campaign in March 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-183\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-183\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Mendham_Borough,_New_Jersey\" title=\"Mendham Borough, New Jersey\">Mendham</a> mayor Christine Serrano Glassner<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-184\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-184\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>160<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> and real estate developer <a href=\"/wiki/Curtis_Bashaw_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Curtis Bashaw (politician)\">Curtis Bashaw</a><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-185\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-185\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>161<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> ran for the Republican nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-cruz&#95;186-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-cruz-186\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>162<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> On June 4, 2024, Bashaw won the Republican primary in an <a href=\"/wiki/Upset_(competition)\" title=\"Upset (competition)\">upset</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-187\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-187\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>163<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Kim won the election with 53% of the vote.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Democratic primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-ei&#95;188-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ei-188\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>164<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Andy_Kim_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Andy Kim (politician)\">Andy Kim</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>392,602 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>74.83% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Patricia Campos-Medina\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">84,286\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">16.06%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Lawrence_Hamm\" title=\"Lawrence Hamm\">Lawrence Hamm</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">47,796\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">9.11%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>524,684 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-ei&#95;188-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ei-188\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>164<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b>Curtis Bashaw </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>144,869 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>45.57% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Christine Serrano Glassner\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">121,986\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">38.38%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Justin Murphy\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">35,954\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">11.31%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Albert Harshaw\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">15,064\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">4.74%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>317,873 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.0% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in New Jersey<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-gc115&#95;81-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-gc115-81\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>58<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" st