d style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Carlton Bowen\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_American_Party\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Independent American Party\">Independent American</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>914,700</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">464,515\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">83,972\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>62.50%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">31.74%\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">5.74%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah_results_map_by_county.svg/250px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah_results_map_by_county.svg/500px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Curtis:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#FFB2B2; color:#FFB2B2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#C21B18; color:#C21B18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Gleich:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#A5B0FF; color:#A5B0FF;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Utah\" title=\"List of United States senators from Utah\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Mitt_Romney\" title=\"Mitt Romney\">Mitt Romney</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/John_Curtis\" title=\"John Curtis\">John Curtis</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Utah\">2024 United States Senate election in Utah</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Utah\" title=\"List of United States senators from Utah\">List of United States senators from Utah</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Utah\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Utah\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Utah</a></div>\n<p>One-term Republican <a href=\"/wiki/Mitt_Romney\" title=\"Mitt Romney\">Mitt Romney</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Utah\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Utah\">elected in 2018</a> with 62.6% of the vote. On September 13, 2023, Romney announced he would not seek reelection in 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-231\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-231\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>207<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The Republican nominee was <a href=\"/wiki/United_States_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"United States House of Representatives\">U.S. representative</a> <a href=\"/wiki/John_Curtis\" title=\"John Curtis\">John Curtis</a>,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-232\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-232\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>208<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> who defeated <a href=\"/wiki/Riverton,_Utah\" title=\"Riverton, Utah\">Riverton</a> Mayor <a href=\"/wiki/Trent_Staggs\" title=\"Trent Staggs\">Trent Staggs</a>,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-233\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-233\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>209<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> and <a href=\"/wiki/Utah_House_of_Representatives\" title=\"Utah House of Representatives\">state House</a> speaker <a href=\"/wiki/Brad_Wilson_(politician)\" title=\"Brad Wilson (politician)\">Brad Wilson</a>,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-234\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-234\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>210<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> in the primary election.\n</p><p>The Democratic nominee was professional skier <a href=\"/wiki/Caroline_Gleich\" title=\"Caroline Gleich\">Caroline Gleich</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-235\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-235\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>211<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Vermont\">Vermont</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47\" title=\"Edit section: Vermont\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Vermont election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Flag_of_Vermont.svg/60px-Flag_of_Vermont.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Flag_of_Vermont.svg/120px-Flag_of_Vermont.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"800\" data-file-height=\"480\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Vermont\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Vermont\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #DCDCDC;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Bernie_Sanders_2023.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bernie_Sanders_2023.jpg/120px-Bernie_Sanders_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Bernie_Sanders_2023.jpg/250px-Bernie_Sanders_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1310\" data-file-height=\"1745\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Gerald_Malloy_for_US_Senate_Vermont_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gerald_Malloy_for_US_Senate_Vermont_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Gerald_Malloy_for_US_Senate_Vermont_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Gerald_Malloy_for_US_Senate_Vermont_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Gerald_Malloy_for_US_Senate_Vermont_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1410\" data-file-height=\"1881\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Bernie_Sanders\" title=\"Bernie Sanders\">Bernie Sanders</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Gerald Malloy\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>229,429</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">116,512\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>63.16%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">32.07%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><div class=\"switcher-container\"><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_county.svg/250px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"220\" height=\"220\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_county.svg/500px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">County results</span></div><div><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_municipality.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_municipality.svg/250px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"220\" height=\"220\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_municipality.svg/500px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont_results_map_by_municipality.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"810\" /></a></span>\n<span class=\"switcher-label\" style=\"display:none\">Municipality results</span></div></div><div><b>Sanders:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D9D9D9; color:#D9D9D9;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#BDBDBD; color:#BDBDBD;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#969696; color:#969696;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#737373; color:#737373;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#555555; color:#555555;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Malloy:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#FFB2B2; color:#FFB2B2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span><br /><b>Tie:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#CDAFDC; color:#CDAFDC;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span><br /><b>No data/vote:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#000000; color:#000000;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Vermont\" title=\"List of United States senators from Vermont\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Bernie_Sanders\" title=\"Bernie Sanders\">Bernie Sanders</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Bernie_Sanders\" title=\"Bernie Sanders\">Bernie Sanders</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Vermont\">2024 United States Senate election in Vermont</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Vermont\" title=\"List of United States senators from Vermont\">List of United States senators from Vermont</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_election_in_Vermont\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives election in Vermont\">2024 United States House of Representatives election in Vermont</a></div>\n<p>Three-term independent <a href=\"/wiki/Bernie_Sanders\" title=\"Bernie Sanders\">Bernie Sanders</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Vermont\">re-elected in 2018</a> with 67.4% of the vote. He was challenged by artist Cris Ericson, an independent <a href=\"/wiki/Perennial_candidate\" title=\"Perennial candidate\">perennial candidate</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-cevt&#95;236-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-cevt-236\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>212<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Businessman Gerald Malloy, who was the Republican nominee for the Senate in <a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Vermont\" title=\"2022 United States Senate election in Vermont\">2022</a>, secured the Republican nomination unopposed.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-237\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-237\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>213<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Virginia\">Virginia</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=48\" title=\"Edit section: Virginia\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Virginia election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Flag_of_Virginia.svg/60px-Flag_of_Virginia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Flag_of_Virginia.svg/120px-Flag_of_Virginia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"341\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Virginia\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Virginia\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Tim_Kaine_116th_official_portrait_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Tim_Kaine_116th_official_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Tim_Kaine_116th_official_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"111\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Tim_Kaine_116th_official_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Tim_Kaine_116th_official_portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1425\" data-file-height=\"1745\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Hung_Cao,_2022.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Hung_Cao%2C_2022.jpg/120px-Hung_Cao%2C_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Hung_Cao%2C_2022.jpg/250px-Hung_Cao%2C_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1235\" data-file-height=\"1647\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kaine\" title=\"Tim Kaine\">Tim Kaine</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Hung_Cao\" title=\"Hung Cao\">Hung Cao</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>2,314,474</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,961,719\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>54.37%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">45.44%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"133\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"358\" /></a></span><div>County and independent city results<br /><b>Kaine:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#3933e5; color:#3933e5;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span><br /><b>Cao:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Virginia\" title=\"List of United States senators from Virginia\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kaine\" title=\"Tim Kaine\">Tim Kaine</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kaine\" title=\"Tim Kaine\">Tim Kaine</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Virginia\">2024 United States Senate election in Virginia</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Virginia\" title=\"List of United States senators from Virginia\">List of United States senators from Virginia</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Virginia\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Virginia\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Virginia</a></div>\n<p>Two-term Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kaine\" title=\"Tim Kaine\">Tim Kaine</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Virginia\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Virginia\">reelected in 2018</a> with 57.0% of the vote. On January 20, 2023, he confirmed he was running for reelection to a third term.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-238\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-238\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>214<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Governor_of_Virginia\" title=\"Governor of Virginia\">Governor</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Glenn_Youngkin\" title=\"Glenn Youngkin\">Glenn Youngkin</a>, who would be term-limited in 2025, was considered a possible Republican candidate.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-239\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-239\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>215<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>On July 18, 2023, Navy veteran <a href=\"/wiki/Hung_Cao\" title=\"Hung Cao\">Hung Cao</a> announced he would run as a Republican. Cao unsuccessfully ran for the <a href=\"/wiki/U.S._House_of_Representatives\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"U.S. House of Representatives\">U.S. House of Representatives</a> against Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Jennifer_Wexton\" title=\"Jennifer Wexton\">Jennifer Wexton</a> in 2022.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-240\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-240\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>216<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Kaine defeated Cao 54% to 45%.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-241\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-241\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>217<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-242\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-242\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>218<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-243\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-243\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>219<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Hung_Cao\" title=\"Hung Cao\">Hung Cao</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>168,868 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>61.79% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Scott Parkinson\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">29,940\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">10.95%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Eddie Garcia\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">26,777\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">9.80%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Chuck Smith\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">24,108\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">8.82%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Jonathan Emord\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">23,614\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">8.64%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>273,307 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\">\n<caption>2024 United States Senate election in Virginia<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-244\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-244\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>220<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 130px\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1038841319\" /><span class=\"rt-commentedText tooltip tooltip-dotted\" title=\"Change in percentage value since previous election\">±%</span>\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9; width:5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Kaine\" title=\"Tim Kaine\">Tim Kaine</a> (incumbent) </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>2,417,115 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>54.37% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right; margin-right:0.5em\"><b>−2.63% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit; background-color: #E81B23; width: 5px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width: 130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Hung_Cao\" title=\"Hung Cao\">Hung Cao</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">2,019,911\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">45.44%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right; margin-right: 0.5em\">+4.44%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: white; width: 2px;\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" colspan=\"2\"><a href=\"/wiki/Write-in_candidate\" title=\"Write-in candidate\">Write-in</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">8,509\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">0.19%\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">+0.03%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>4,445,535 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\">N/A\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color: #0044C9;\">\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" colspan=\"5\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(US)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Democratic Party (US)\">Democratic</a> <b>hold</b>\n</th></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Washington\">Washington</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=49\" title=\"Edit section: Washington\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:300px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">Washington election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flag_of_Washington.svg/60px-Flag_of_Washington.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"31\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Flag_of_Washington.svg/120px-Flag_of_Washington.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1600\" data-file-height=\"1000\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Washington\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in Washington\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Maria_Cantwell_(cropped).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Maria_Cantwell_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Maria_Cantwell_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"109\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Maria_Cantwell_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Maria_Cantwell_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"505\" data-file-height=\"628\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/120px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/3x4.svg/250px-3x4.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"3\" data-file-height=\"4\" /></span></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Candidate\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Maria_Cantwell\" title=\"Maria Cantwell\">Maria Cantwell</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Raul Garcia\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>2,252,577</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">1,549,187\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>59.09%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">40.64%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"198\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"535\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Cantwell:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#7996e2; color:#7996e2;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#584cde; color:#584cde;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span><br /><b>Garcia:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Washington\" title=\"List of United States senators from Washington\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Maria_Cantwell\" title=\"Maria Cantwell\">Maria Cantwell</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Maria_Cantwell\" title=\"Maria Cantwell\">Maria Cantwell</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in Washington\">2024 United States Senate election in Washington</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Washington\" title=\"List of United States senators from Washington\">List of United States senators from Washington</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Washington\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Washington\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in Washington</a></div>\n<p>Four-term Democrat <a href=\"/wiki/Maria_Cantwell\" title=\"Maria Cantwell\">Maria Cantwell</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_Washington\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in Washington\">reelected in 2018</a> with 58.4% of the vote.\n</p><p>Emergency room physician Raul Garcia announced that he would run as a Republican.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-245\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-245\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>221<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\"></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"West_Virginia\">West Virginia</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=2024_United_States_Senate_elections&amp;action=edit&amp;section=50\" title=\"Edit section: West Virginia\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1315121714\" /><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1152813436\" /><table class=\"infobox ib-election infobox-table\" style=\"width:250px\"><caption class=\"infobox-title summary\">West Virginia election</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><span class=\"flagicon\"><span class=\"mw-image-border\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img alt=\"\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Flag_of_West_Virginia.svg/60px-Flag_of_West_Virginia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"26\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Flag_of_West_Virginia.svg/120px-Flag_of_West_Virginia.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"760\" data-file-height=\"400\" /></span></span></span><hr /></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-subheader\"><div style=\"width:100%\"><div style=\"float: left; text-align:left;padding-right:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\">&#8592;&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in West Virginia\">2018</a></div><div style=\"float: right; text-align:right;padding-left:0.5em;width:20%;\" class=\"noprint\"><a href=\"/wiki/2030_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2030 United States Senate election in West Virginia\">2030</a>&#160;&#8594;</div></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\">\n<table style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n\n\n\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #E81B23;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Senator_Jim_Justice_Official_Portrait_with_flags.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Senator_Jim_Justice_Official_Portrait_with_flags.jpg/120px-Senator_Jim_Justice_Official_Portrait_with_flags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"106\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Senator_Jim_Justice_Official_Portrait_with_flags.jpg/250px-Senator_Jim_Justice_Official_Portrait_with_flags.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1530\" data-file-height=\"1970\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td class=\"notheme\" style=\"text-align:center;border-bottom: 6px solid #0044C9;\"><span class=\"notpageimage noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Glenn_Elliott_WV.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Glenn_Elliott_WV.jpg/120px-Glenn_Elliott_WV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Glenn_Elliott_WV.jpg/250px-Glenn_Elliott_WV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"305\" data-file-height=\"406\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Nominee\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Jim_Justice\" title=\"Jim Justice\">Jim Justice</a></b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">Glenn Elliott\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:center\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Party\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><a href=\"/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Democratic Party (United States)\">Democratic</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Popular&#160;vote\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>514,079</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">207,548\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width:75px;text-align:left\">Percentage\n</th>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\"><b>68.75%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">27.76%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg/250px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"222\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg/500px-2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"719\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Justice:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#E27F7F; color:#E27F7F;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#D72F30; color:#D72F30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#C21B18; color:#C21B18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_West_Virginia\" title=\"List of United States senators from West Virginia\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Manchin\" title=\"Joe Manchin\">Joe Manchin</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Independent_politician\" title=\"Independent politician\">Independent</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Jim_Justice\" title=\"Jim Justice\">Jim Justice</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"2024 United States Senate election in West Virginia\">2024 United States Senate election in West Virginia</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_West_Virginia\" title=\"List of United States senators from West Virginia\">List of United States senators from West Virginia</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"2024 United States House of Representatives elections in West Virginia\">2024 United States House of Representatives elections in West Virginia</a></div>\n<p>Independent <a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Manchin\" title=\"Joe Manchin\">Joe Manchin</a>, who was elected as a Democrat, was <a href=\"/wiki/2018_United_States_Senate_election_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"2018 United States Senate election in West Virginia\">re-elected in 2018</a> with 49.6% of the vote. On November 9, 2023, Manchin announced he would not seek re-election.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-ManchinWV&#95;70-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-ManchinWV-70\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>48<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Since Manchin announced his retirement, all major outlets rated this seat as expected to flip to GOP control, which would put this seat in Republican hands for the first time in <a href=\"/wiki/1956_United_States_Senate_elections#West_Virginia_(special)\" title=\"1956 United States Senate elections\">68 years</a>.\n</p><p>Popular <a href=\"/wiki/Governor_of_West_Virginia\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Governor of West Virginia\">governor</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Jim_Justice\" title=\"Jim Justice\">Jim Justice</a> easily defeated U.S. representative <a href=\"/wiki/Alex_Mooney\" title=\"Alex Mooney\">Alex Mooney</a><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-246\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-246\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>222<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> in the Republican primary.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/Wheeling,_West_Virginia\" title=\"Wheeling, West Virginia\">Wheeling</a> mayor <a href=\"/wiki/Glenn_Elliott_(politician)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Glenn Elliott (politician)\">Glenn Elliott</a>, who had Manchin's endorsement,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-247\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-247\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>223<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> defeated <a href=\"/wiki/Community_organizer\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Community organizer\">community organizer</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/U.S._Marine_Corps\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"U.S. Marine Corps\">U.S. Marine Corps</a> veteran <a href=\"/wiki/Zachary_Shrewsbury\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Zachary Shrewsbury\">Zachary Shrewsbury</a> and former coal executive <a href=\"/wiki/Don_Blankenship\" title=\"Don Blankenship\">Don Blankenship</a> in the primary for the Democratic Party nomination.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-248\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-248\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>224<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Due to West Virginia's heavy Republican lean, the absence of Manchin, Justice's personal popularity, and being held concurrently with a <a href=\"/wiki/2024_United_States_presidential_election\" title=\"2024 United States presidential election\">presidential race</a> in a state in which <a href=\"/wiki/Donald_Trump\" title=\"Donald Trump\">Donald Trump</a> was expected to win in a landslide, a Republican pickup for this seat was considered a foregone conclusion in 2024.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-249\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-249\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>225<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Justice was sworn in as a Senator on January 14, 2025, giving elected Republicans control of both of West Virginia’s Senate seats for the first time since 1931 and giving the state an entirely Republican congressional delegation for the first time since 1923.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-250\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-250\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>y<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> This was the first time since the <a href=\"/wiki/1956_United_States_Senate_special_election_in_West_Virginia\" title=\"1956 United States Senate special election in West Virginia\">1956 special election</a> that a Republican won West Virginia's Class I Senate Seat.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Democratic primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-NYTPrimary&#95;251-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NYTPrimary-251\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>226<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Democratic_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Democratic Party\">Democratic</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b>Glenn Elliott </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>46,176 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>45.40% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Democratic_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Democratic Party\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Zach Shrewsbury\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">36,754\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">36.14%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#0044C9;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Democratic_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Democratic Party\">Democratic</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Don_Blankenship\" title=\"Don Blankenship\">Don Blankenship</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">18,778\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">18.46%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:right;\">Total votes\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>101,708 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;\"><b>100.00% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Republican primary results<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-NYTPrimary&#95;251-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-NYTPrimary-251\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>226<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align:left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Jim_Justice\" title=\"Jim Justice\">Jim Justice</a> </b>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>138,307 </b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right;margin-right:0.5em\"><b>61.84% </b>\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\"><a href=\"/wiki/Alex_Mooney\" title=\"Alex Mooney\">Alex Mooney</a>\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">59,348\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">26.54%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Bryan Bird\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">7,001\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">3.13%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Bryan McKinney\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">6,573\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">2.94%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"text-align: left; font-weight:normal; color:inherit; background:inherit;\" class=\"fn\">Zane Lawhorn\n</th>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">4,517\n</td>\n<td style=\"text-align:right\">2.02%\n</td></tr>\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:2px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><a href=\"/wiki/West_Virginia_Republican_Party\" title=\"West Virginia Republican Party\">Republican</a>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" style=\"