citation news cs1\">Balz, Dan (September 13, 2023). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/09/13/mitt-romney-senate-reelection/\">\"Mitt Romney says he will not seek a second term in the Senate\"</a>. <i>Washington Post</i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230913213815/https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/09/13/mitt-romney-senate-reelection/\">Archived</a> from the original on September 13, 2023<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">September 13,</span> 2023</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Washington+Post&amp;rft.atitle=Mitt+Romney+says+he+will+not+seek+a+second+term+in+the+Senate&amp;rft.date=2023-09-13&amp;rft.au=Balz%2C+Dan&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fpolitics%2F2023%2F09%2F13%2Fmitt-romney-senate-reelection%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3A2024+United+States+Senate+elections\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-232\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-232\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFAerts2024\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Aerts, Lindsay (January 2, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ksltv.com/611775/rep-john-curtis-officially-running-for-romneys-senate-seat/\">\"Rep. John Curtis officially running for Romney's senate seat\"</a>. <i>KSL TV</i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240103001925/https://ksltv.com/611775/rep-john-curtis-officially-running-for-romneys-senate-seat/\">Archived</a> from the original on January 3, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">January 2,</sp